infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What the padlock guarantees — and what it does not
  desc TLS seals the channel; it makes no promise about the endpoints
  compares
    - label TLS guarantees
      children
        - label Confidentiality
          desc Nobody on the wire can read the data
        - label Integrity
          desc Tampering in transit is detected
        - label Authentication
          desc Server proves it owns the domain (CA cert)
    - label TLS does NOT guarantee
      children
        - label Site is trustworthy
          desc A scam site can hold a valid padlock
        - label Your device is safe
          desc Endpoint compromise is a separate problem
        - label Data at rest is protected
          desc TLS covers transit, not storage on the server
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
